Sure! Below is a simple example of an HTML “card” that rotates 180 degrees around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Hover‑Rotate Card</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Container that holds the card – gives perspective so the rotation looks 3D */
.card-wrapper {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 800px;          /* How far the viewer is from the card */
  margin: 50px auto;           /* Center horizontally */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform .6s ease;   /* Smooth animation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;     /* Needed for 3D transforms */
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card .front,
.card .back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;      /* Hide the reverse side while rotated */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
}

/* Back side – rotated 180° so it’s initially hidden */
.card .back {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
  background: #f8f8f8;
}

/* Hover effect – flip the card */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);        /* Flip the whole card */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="front">Front Side</div>
    <div class="back">Back Side</div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3D perspective (`perspective: 800px`) so the rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | Holds both sides, has `transform-style: preserve-3d` so child elements keep their 3D context. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Each side is absolutely positioned on top of each other. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that’s turned away from the viewer. |
| `.back` | Rotated 180° initially so it’s hidden until the parent flips. |
| `.card:hover` | Rotates the entire card 180° around the Y‑axis. |

You can replace the text inside `.front` and `.back` with images, icons, or any content you like. Adjust the `perspective`, `transition`, and `border-radius` values to fit your design. Enjoy!
